WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:03.160
Foreside Fiasco

00:03.290 --> 00:06.520
Written, read, and lived by Sam Peret.

00:08.170 --> 00:11.960
Dedicated to Steve, Lurana and the Foreside Manor.

00:13.270 --> 00:15.900
It started one morning so peaceful and bright,

00:15.950 --> 00:20.060
At Steve and Lurana’s, the mood was just right.

00:20.270 --> 00:23.460
A cozy old house with sunlight to spare,

00:23.970 --> 00:27.680
Warm coffee aromas danced through the air.

00:28.610 --> 00:32.740
And when the work was finished, the day nearly done,

00:32.850 --> 00:36.580
The Burgies were poured, perhaps more than one.

00:36.710 --> 00:39.480
The perfect way to end the day,

00:39.770 --> 00:43.500
Everything was feeling A.O.K.

00:44.490 --> 00:48.180
Then Lurana remembered, “Oh wait, in the nook!”

00:48.370 --> 00:51.720
A box had been waiting, she gave it a look.

00:52.290 --> 00:55.920
“Warm seat! Air dryer! A luxury spray!

00:56.170 --> 00:59.220
We’ve truly gone fancy with this bidet!”

00:59.610 --> 01:03.060
“The plumbers are coming,” Lurana did say,

01:03.330 --> 01:07.120
But Sam waved his hand, “We’ll do it today!”

01:07.690 --> 01:10.960
Steve yawned and smiled, “I’m off to bed,”

01:11.330 --> 01:15.380
While Sam rolled his sleeves and scratched his head.

01:16.770 --> 01:20.040
Out came the wrench, the shiny new seat.

01:20.190 --> 01:23.320
“This bidet will make your bathroom elite!”

01:23.390 --> 01:26.880
He twisted, he turned, and gave it a shove,

01:27.090 --> 01:30.580
A confident handyman, sort of, thereof.

01:32.410 --> 01:35.260
Then all of a sudden arose such a clatter,

01:35.310 --> 01:39.020
With Lurana screaming, “What is the matter?!”

01:39.430 --> 01:42.940
Sam held the pipe, water shooting up high.

01:43.030 --> 01:46.560
The valve was broken! Oh me, oh my!

01:47.450 --> 01:50.520
Steve rushed downstairs, hair all askew,

01:50.570 --> 01:54.060
As drips from the chandelier shimmered like dew.

01:54.110 --> 01:57.420
Towels were flying, the floor got all wet,

01:57.570 --> 02:01.660
A scene they would sure never forget!

02:02.470 --> 02:07.480
The next morning the plumbers arrived, their tools in a queue,

02:07.870 --> 02:10.840
Now the bidet sparkles, clean and new.

02:11.250 --> 02:13.900
Steve, Lurana, and Sam all say,

02:14.070 --> 02:18.040
“Next time, we’ll wait for the pros — okay?”
